<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>1-for-20 Share Combination and Press Release</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As previously disclosed in the report on Form
6-K filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (the &ldquo;<B>SEC</B>&rdquo;) on February 4, 2026 by Jin Medical International
Limited, an exempted company incorporated in the Cayman Islands (the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;), at the Company&rsquo;s extraordinary
general meeting held on January 30, 2026 (the &ldquo;<B>EGM</B>&rdquo;), the Company&rsquo;s shareholders approved up to three share consolidations
of the Company&rsquo;s authorized and issued ordinary shares within two years from the date of the EGM at the pre-determined consolidation
ratios approved at the EGM, to be effected if the closing market price of the Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares is less than US$1.00.
The Company&rsquo;s board of directors (the &ldquo;<B>Board</B>&rdquo;) was authorized, in its sole discretion, to determine whether and
when to effect any such share consolidation and to implement any such consolidation in accordance with the shareholders&rsquo; approval.&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">On February 3, 2026, the Board approved a combination&#8239;of
all of the Company&rsquo;s authorized and issued Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares at a ratio of one-for-twenty (1-for-20)
(the &ldquo;<B>Share Consolidation</B>&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">In addition, as previously disclosed in the report
on Form 6-K filed by the Company with the SEC on February 4, 2026, the Company has reclassified its share capital from a single class
of ordinary shares to a dual class of Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares, effective as of the date of the EGM (the &ldquo;<B>Reclassification</B>&rdquo;).
As a result of the Reclassification and the Share Consolidation, the Company&rsquo;s authorized share capital became US$50,000 divided
into 45,000,000 Class A ordinary shares of a par value of US$0.001 each, and 5,000,000 Class B ordinary shares of a par value of US$0.001
each.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Reclassification and the Share Consolidation
became effective with The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC (&ldquo;<B>Nasdaq</B>&rdquo;) on March 16, 2026 at 09:00 a.m., Eastern Time (the &ldquo;<B>Effective
Time</B>&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">At the Effective Time, every twenty (20) shares
of the Company&rsquo;s authorized and issued ordinary shares (including all Class A ordinary shares and Class B ordinary shares) were
combined into one (1) share of ordinary share in the respective share class. The number of issued and outstanding shares of Class A ordinary
shares was therefore reduced from 136,547,100 shares to 6,827,355 shares, and the number of issued and outstanding shares of Class B ordinary
shares was therefore reduced from 20,000,000 shares to 1,000,000 shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company believes the Share Consolidation is
a proactive measure as part of the Company&rsquo;s strategic plan to maintain compliance with continued listing requirements of Nasdaq,
while it is also intended for strengthening the Company&rsquo;s long-term capital structure.&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company&rsquo;s Class A ordinary shares will
continue to trade on Nasdaq under the existing symbol &ldquo;ZJYL&rdquo; and will begin trading on a consolidation-adjusted basis as of
the Effective Date. The new CUSIP number for the Class A ordinary shares following the Share Consolidation is G5140V120.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">On March 11, 2026, the Company published a press
release entitled &ldquo;<I>Jin Medical International Ltd. Announces 1-for-20 Share Combination as Part of Strategic Nasdaq Compliance
Initiative</I>&rdquo;, a copy of which is attached hereto as Exhibit 99.1.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">This Report shall be deemed to be incorporated
by reference into the registration statement on&nbsp;<A HREF="http://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1837821/000121390025057795/ea0246531-f3_jinmedical.htm">Form F-3</A>&nbsp;(File No. 333-288314), and to be a part thereof from the date on which this current report on Form 6-K is filed, to the extent
not superseded by documents or reports subsequently filed or furnished.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>


